---
// Signed-out `/`. Macrostructure 02 Long Document, nav N6 Newspaper masthead,
// footer Ft5 Statement. This is the one page that loads Anton.
//
// Copy is rewritten from idea-notes.md § Główny problem and the PRD. It is NOT
// from README.md — that file is still the unmodified 10x Astro Starter readme
// and describes Astro, not this product.
//
// Every claim below is checkable. There are no metrics, no testimonials and no
// logos, because the product has none and inventing them is the fastest way to
// make a page read as generated.
---

<main id="main" class="poster">
  <header>
    {
      /* Account actions sit in the top row, not in the section nav. Sharing one
        wrapping row with three section links pushed them onto the last line on
        a phone, which put "Sign in" at the bottom of the masthead — the one
        place a visitor should never have to hunt for it. */
    }
    <div class="mast">
      <p class="mast-name">
        <a class="wordmark" data-t="about-books" href="/"><span>about-books</span></a><span class="mast-no">No 01</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mast-auth label">
        <a href="/auth/signin">Sign in</a>
        <a class="primary" href="/auth/signup">Sign up</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rule-thick"></div>
    <div class="rule-thin"></div>
    <nav class="mast-nav label" aria-label="Main">
      <span class="nav-links">
        <a href="#problem">The problem</a>
        <a href="#what">What it does</a>
        <a href="#wont">What it won’t do</a>
      </span>
      <span class="mast-tag">Private by default · Your notes, nobody else’s</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="rule-thin"></div>
  </header>

  <div class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="label eyebrow">A reading companion for books put down and picked up again</p>
      <h1 class="head">
        {
          /* The ghost layer is generated content, so it never reaches the
            accessibility tree and cannot be selected as text. */
        }
        <span class="line" data-t="Put it down."><span>Put it down.</span></span>
        <span class="line red" data-t="Pick it up."><span>Pick it up.</span></span>
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="aside">
      <p>
        Three weeks pass. You open the book and you have <strong>no idea who she is</strong>, or why he owes her
        anything. That is not a comprehension problem — you understood it perfectly at the time. It is a recall problem,
        and it only shows up on the way back in.
      </p>
      <p>
        So write the cast down as you go: names, a line each, and <span class="say">who is what to whom</span>. Then the
        way back in is a glance instead of a search.
      </p>
      <p class="cta">
        <a class="cta-link" href="/auth/signup">Start a library</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="problem" class="band">
    <h2 class="band-head">The problem is the gap, not the book</h2>
    <p>
      Reading gets interrupted. A chapter on Tuesday, three pages on Sunday, nothing for a fortnight. The plot survives
      that. The cast does not — the second cousin introduced on page 40 is gone by page 200, and the only way back is to
      flick through looking for a name you cannot quite remember.
    </p>
    <p>
      Note-taking apps do not help, because in a note the relationships are prose. You cannot look up who is whose
      sister when the answer is buried in a paragraph you wrote a month ago.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what" class="band">
    <h2 class="band-head">What it does</h2>
    <ul class="does">
      <li><span class="label">Books</span> A list of what you are reading, and what you have finished.</li>
      <li><span class="label">Cast</span> Every character, with a line about who they are, added in seconds.</li>
      <li>
        <span class="label">Relations</span> Named connections between them — family, ally, antagonist, romantic, or a word
        you invent for one particular book.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="label">Recall</span> The whole cast and its connections on one screen, so returning after a gap is a
        glance.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="wont" class="band">
    <h2 class="band-head">What it won’t do</h2>
    <p>
      There is no progress tracking, no page counter, no percentage and no streak. Nothing here measures how much you
      read or how often. It is a notebook for a cast, not a fitness tracker for books.
    </p>
    <p>There is no feed, nothing shared and nothing public. Your library is visible to you and to nobody else.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="close">
    <div class="rule-thin"></div>
    <p class="statement">Write the cast down. Come back whenever you like.</p>
    <p class="label">
      <a href="/auth/signup">Sign up</a> · <a href="/auth/signin">Sign in</a>
    </p>
  </footer>
</main>

<style>
  .poster {
    --gutter: max(var(--space-md), env(safe-area-inset-left));
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-2xl);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  /* ── Masthead ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .mast {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    padding-block: var(--space-md) var(--space-xs);
  }
  .mast-name {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  .mast-no {
    margin-inline-start: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  /* Account actions. 44px tap targets even though they are label-sized text —
     these are the two most important controls on the page for a visitor. */
  .mast-auth {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }
  .mast-auth a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .mast-auth a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .mast-auth .primary {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* The pair is the device. A single rule reads as an ordinary underline. */
  .rule-thick {
    height: var(--rule-w-thick);
    background: var(--ink);
  }
  .rule-thin {
    height: var(--rule-w);
    background: var(--ink);
    margin-block-start: 2px;
  }

  .mast-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-md);
    padding-block: var(--space-xs);
  }
  .nav-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
  }
  /* The tagline is masthead furniture, not navigation — it drops under the
     links when the row cannot hold both. */
  .mast-tag {
    color: var(--faint);
  }
  .mast-nav a {
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .mast-nav a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
  }
  @container (min-width: 52rem) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: end;
    }
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-md);
  }

  .head {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .line {
    position: relative;
    font-family: var(--font-poster);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-poster);
    line-height: 0.9;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .line::before {
    content: attr(data-t);
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: -0.055em;
    inset-inline-start: -0.035em;
    color: var(--ghost);
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .line > span {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .line.red > span {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .aside {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }
  .aside p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .aside strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .say {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
  }
  .cta-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding-inline: var(--space-md);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cta-link:hover {
    background: var(--ink-2);
  }

  /* ── Bands ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .band {
    border-block-start: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    padding-block: var(--space-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .band-head {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  .band p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .does {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .does li {
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .does .label {
    display: block;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-block-end: 2px;
  }

  /* ── Ft5 Statement ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .close {
    padding-block-start: var(--space-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .statement {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    max-width: 32ch;
  }
  .close .label {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .close a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .close a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
